//Interface---An interface defines a contract that a class must follow.
//it is like set of rules a class have to follow.

/*In an interface a public method is declared without implementation and now every other class 
which is implementing the interface must implement it with its own functionality
A class can implement multiple interfaces
*/


interface Drivable {
    public function drive();
}

interface Chargeable {
    public function charge();
}

class ElectricCar implements Drivable, Chargeable {

    public function drive() {
        echo "Driving";
    }

    public function charge() {
        echo "Charging";
    }

}// Any class implementing Chargeable must have a public charge() method.


